{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-8126" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073357/assets/7bfcc5c729475256b70211bcf18e94b605e4486790b13794eaa46cce4f6461bb.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe triangle $△ABC$ is shown above. Which of the following is $△{A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′},$ the image of $△ABC$ under the action of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073357/state.json" "file_sha256" "7bf44543c5b6a4d1cdce4c4e4b24a4d83a81681adbd46e7e4ddd7cdbdb600526"} {"question" "q-8126" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the image of $T$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $△ABC:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -4 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $△{A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}$ are $(-3,-1),(-4,0),(-2,2)$, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073357/assets/548c907226db9cbdc8fb4dd18c74f3a2001ba7d90973c6f433f67b3e6b87fd29.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073357/state.json" "file_sha256" "7bf44543c5b6a4d1cdce4c4e4b24a4d83a81681adbd46e7e4ddd7cdbdb600526"} {"question" "q-8126" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value