ence/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073357/assets/548c907226db9cbdc8fb4dd18c74f3a2001ba7d90973c6f433f67b3e6b87fd29.png"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073357/state.json" "file_sha256" "7bf44543c5b6a4d1cdce4c4e4b24a4d83a81681adbd46e7e4ddd7cdbdb600526"} {"question" "q-77702" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ has endpoints at $A(-1,2)$ and $B(1,1).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding endpoints of $\\overset{―}{{A}^{′}{B}^{′}}$, the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073357/state.json" "file_sha256" "7bf44543c5b6a4d1cdce4c4e4b24a4d83a81681adbd46e7e4ddd7cdbdb600526"} {"question" "q-77702" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${A}^{′}(0,5)$ and ${B}^{′}(3,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073357/state.json" "file_sha256" "7bf44543c5b6a4d1cdce4c4e4b24a4d83a81681adbd46e7e4ddd7cdbdb600526"} {"question"