B}^{′}($ \n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}}\n$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073357/state.json" "file_sha256" "7bf44543c5b6a4d1cdce4c4e4b24a4d83a81681adbd46e7e4ddd7cdbdb600526"} {"question" "q-275723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the image of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${A}^{′}(2,3)$ and ${B}^{′}(-2,-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073357/state.json" "file_sha256" "7bf44543c5b6a4d1cdce4c4e4b24a4d83a81681adbd46e7e4ddd7cdbdb600526"} {"question" "q-275723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073357/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e60df9246148524152d27f56dbf020d0ccac34c1ac9f91158315a5a204b1b814"} {"question" "q-275723" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073357/state.json" "file_sha256" "7bf44543c5b6a4d1cdce4c4e4b24a4d83a81681adbd46e7e4ddd7cdbdb600526"} {"question" "q-275723" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "