wer.type/math "-1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073357/state.json" "file_sha256" "7bf44543c5b6a4d1cdce4c4e4b24a4d83a81681adbd46e7e4ddd7cdbdb600526"} {"question" "q-281528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $T$ be the linear transformation with matrix representation $T$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA line segment $\\overset{―}{RS}$ has endpoints at $R(0,2)$ and $S(-1,1).$ What are the coordinates of the corresponding endpoints $\\overset{―}{{R}^{′}{S}^{′}}$, the image of $\\overset{―}{RS}$ under the action of $T?$\n\n${R}^{′}($ \n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,$ and $\\,{S}^{′}($ \n{{field-3}}, \n{{field-4}}\n$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073357/state.json" "file_sha256" "7bf44543c5b6a4d1cdce4c4e4b24a4d83a81681adbd46e7e4ddd7cdbdb600526"} {"question" "q-281528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the image of $\\overset{―}{RS}$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the endpoints of $\\overset{―}{RS}:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective endpoints of the image are ${R}^{′}(2,0)$ and ${S}^{′}(-1,-1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073357/state.json" "file_sha256" "7bf44543c5b6a4d1cdce4c4e4b24a4d83a81681adbd46e7e4ddd7cdbdb600526"} {"question" "q-281528" "fi