of $PQR:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 16 & -10 \\\\ 6 & -2 & 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of $△{P}^{′}{Q}^{′}{R}^{′}$ are ${P}^{′}(0,6),$\n${Q}^{′}(16,-2),$ ${R}^{′}(-10,8).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073357/state.json" "file_sha256" "7bf44543c5b6a4d1cdce4c4e4b24a4d83a81681adbd46e7e4ddd7cdbdb600526"} {"question" "q-281560" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073357/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e60df9246148524152d27f56dbf020d0ccac34c1ac9f91158315a5a204b1b814"} {"question" "q-281560" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073357/state.json" "file_sha256" "7bf44543c5b6a4d1cdce4c4e4b24a4d83a81681adbd46e7e4ddd7cdbdb600526"} {"question" "q-281560" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073357/state.json" "file_sha256" "7bf44543c5b6a4d1cdce4c4e4b24a4d83a81681adbd46e7e4ddd7cdbdb600526"} {"question" "q-281560" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear